FoamFile { version 2.0; format ascii; class dictionary; object fvSchemes; }
// CLASS DEFAULT, carried unchanged from cases/ansys_verification/VMFL054-R3/case/system/
// fvSchemes -- the same flow class (steady laminar lid-driven cavity, simpleFoam/SIMPLEC)
// on which this lab already measured a CONVERGING Roache triple (p = 1.195,
// GCI_fine = 0.0356 %).  NOT tuned for VMFL078.
//
// div(phi,U) is UNLIMITED central differencing on purpose: a limiter is nonlinear in the
// solution and destroys the clean asymptotic order a Roache triple is built to measure.
// The disclosed price is stated a priori in PREREGISTRATION.md sec.5: the cell Reynolds
// number U*dx/nu is 31.25 / 15.63 / 7.81 at L1 / L2 / L3, above the CD monotonicity
// limit of 2 at every level, so wiggles are EXPECTED at L1 and are DISCRETISATION ERROR
// that refinement removes -- which is precisely the quantity the triple measures.
// THE SCHEME IS FROZEN ACROSS ALL THREE LEVELS.  Changing it mid-family voids the triple;
// a change is a successor registration (VMFL078-R2), never a repair.
ddtSchemes      { default steadyState; }
gradSchemes     { default Gauss linear; }
divSchemes
{
    default         none;
    div(phi,U)      bounded Gauss linear;
    div((nuEff*dev2(T(grad(U))))) Gauss linear;
}
laplacianSchemes { default Gauss linear corrected; }
interpolationSchemes { default linear; }
snGradSchemes   { default corrected; }
